{"name":"Gunny Sack","hex":"#dcd3bc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gunny sack","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sack made from burlap, used for agricultural produce."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gunny_sack"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gunny sack","blocks":[{"text":"A gunny sack, also known as a gunny shoe, burlap sack, hessian sack or tow sack, is a large sack, traditionally made of burlap formed from jute, hemp, sisal, or other natural fibres, usually in the crude spun form of tow. Modern-day versions of these sacks are often made from synthetic fabrics, such as polypropylene."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Hemp-sack%2C_Asabukuro%2C_Japan.jpg/330px-Hemp-sack%2C_Asabukuro%2C_Japan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gunny_sack"},{"title":"Gunnery sergeant","blocks":[{"text":"Gunnery sergeant (GySgt) is the seventh enlisted rank in the United States Marine Corps, above staff sergeant and below master sergeant and first sergeant, and is a staff non-commissioned officer (SNCO). It has a pay grade of E-7. Gunnery sergeants are commonly referred by the nickname \"Gunny\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gunnery_sergeant"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Thousands_of_bean_bags.jpg/500px-Thousands_of_bean_bags.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Thousands_of_bean_bags.jpg/1280px-Thousands_of_bean_bags.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Thousands_of_bean_bags.jpg/500px-Thousands_of_bean_bags.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stacks of coffee bags, Ethiopia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AT